# security — privacy/security tooling pack (#25, PROPOSAL §14). Firewalls,
# per-app outbound control, password + hardware-token management, Secure Boot
# tooling, and mesh/VPN clients. Installed ONLINE on demand (official repos via
# pacman) — nothing baked or stashed (design pivot #42); only this name-list
# rides in the image as TEXT.
#
# SERVICES ARE NOT AUTO-ENABLED (§14). A firewall or mesh daemon that came up
# silently on install could lock the user out or change the network posture
# without consent. post-add installs the members, drops any ii-OWNED ruleset
# files (additive, never an in-place vendor edit), and PRINTS enable hints
# (mirroring ii-post-install's fail-soft `try` posture) — it records NOTHING as
# enabled. post-remove removes the ii-owned rulesets. ufw and firewalld are both
# offered; the user picks one and enables it from the printed hint.
#meta:type security
ufw
firewalld
opensnitch
keepassxc
yubikey-manager
yubikey-personalization
sbctl
tailscale
wireguard-tools
